                                     AGILE
Agile is a way of working where a team does its work in small pieces, finishing a few at a time, instead of planning one big project.
Big plans can go wrong, because things change while the work is happening. With small pieces, a team finishes something, checks it, and adjusts before starting the next piece.

How does Agile work?
Plan ----> Develop ----->Review ----> Improve and plan again ---> Make adjustments and start the next cycle

Important Agile terms
Agile Team -->  People working together using Agile
Backlog	-->     List of pending work
Story -->       A small piece of work or requirement
Iteration	-->   A fixed period in which selected work is completed
Scrum	-->       An Agile framework that uses iterations
Kanban -->	    A way to visualize and manage work on a board

Why do companies use Agile?
- Requirements can change frequently.
- Teams can deliver work in smaller portions.
- Customers can provide feedback regularly.
- Teams can adjust priorities.
- Progress is easier to visualize.


