                                       Request

A Request is a work submission made by a user to another team or department, asking them to perform some work or resolve an issue.
          Request = someone asking for work that wasn’t in the plan.
A submitted request becomes an issue in the request queue.
Subject is the only required field
When you submit the request, the draft automatically deletes and cannot be restored.

Why do we need Requests?
Without a request process:
- Users may send requirements through emails.
- Requests may get missed.
- Teams may not know who submitted the request.
- Tracking request status becomes difficult.
With Workfront Requests:
- Requests are submitted in one place.
- Teams can review incoming requests.
- Request status can be tracked.
- Requests can be converted into actionable work when appropriate.


